Aim:-
Write a program to demonstrate dictionary & related functions in python

Algorithm:-
1. Start
2. Create an empty dictionary phonebook
3. Input name from the user
4. Input phone number from the user
5. Store name and number in the dictionary → phonebook[name] = number
6. Display the phonebook
7. Input a name to search
8. Use get() to find the phone number
9. If the name exists, display the phone number; otherwise display "Contact not found"
10. Input a name to delete
11. Remove the name from the dictionary using pop()
12. Display the updated phonebook
13. End

Code:-
phonebook = {}
name = input("Enter name: ")
number = input("Enter phone number: ")
phonebook[name] = number
print("Phonebook:", phonebook)
search = input("Enter name to search: ")
print("Phone number:", phonebook.get(search, "Contact not found"))
delete = input("Enter name to delete: ")
phonebook.pop(delete, "Contact not found")
print("Updated phonebook:", phonebook)

Output:-
Enter name: prakash
Enter phone number: 1234567890
Phonebook: {'prakash': '1234567890'}
Enter name to search: prakash
Phone number: 1234567890
Enter name to delete: prakash
Updated phonebook: {}
